      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "An observance that is binding. The sloka occurs in Mud. II.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "The fig. is अर्थान्तरन्यास.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 14. पिण्ड—a ball of rice. Cf. ननु पश्य आश्वासितः पिशाचोपि",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "भोजनेन’ । Vik. II. This metaphorically means ‘when bribed.’",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "मृदङ्ग—Tabors were originally made of earth. मुखलेपेन—refers",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "to the practice of applying kneaded flour to a Mṛdanga before",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "it is played upon. The fig. is अर्थान्तरन्यास.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 15. स्वभरण०—solely bent upon, exerting themselves for.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Cf. जठरं को न बिभर्ति केवलम् । H. अग्रणीः—The leader of; अग्रं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "नयतीति fr. अग्र+नी+क्विप् (०) by ‘सत्सूद्विष &c.’ Pân. III. 2. 61.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "The न is changed to ण after अग्र and ग्राम by the Vârt. अग्रग्रामाभ्यां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "नयतेर्णो वाच्यः । दुष्पूर०—दुःखेन पूर्यते इति; shows the extreme selfish-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "ness of Vádava. वाडवः—The submarine fire; also called Aurva;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "see sl. 76. जीमूतः—जीवनस्य मूतः—पटबन्धः जीमूतः, a comp. of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "पृषोदरादि class. संभृत—qualifies संताप; caused or intensified by.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "विच्छित्तये—for entirely removing or annihilating. The dat. is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "तादर्थ्ये by the Várt. तादर्थ्ये चतुर्थी वाच्या । The cloud is mentioned",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "here as the type of सत्.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 16. In this sl. a minister and a poet are described as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "having a similar function to do, by epithets which are slishta.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "दूरात्—(1) from afar; may also be metaphorical; (2) far apart",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "i. e. by using words in a slishta or secondary ( लाक्षणिक) sense; by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "presenting a striking picture to the mind far beyond the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "conception of ordinary men. अर्थ—(1) wealth or a political end;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "(2) the intended sense. अपशब्दं त्यक्त्वा—Avoiding wrangling;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "or offensive words; or take the whole as चापशब्दं the twanging",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "sound of the bow. i. e. achieving lofty aims by a wise stroke of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "policy without having recourse to war.; (2) faulty or offensive",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "expressions, wrong words. सत्सभा—(1) assemblies of good ( or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "politically clever ) people, political bodies; (2) assemblies of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "learned ( able to appreciate सहृदय ) men. पदम्—(1) step; ( 2 )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "words. लोकचित्त०—(1) by consulting public opinion; (2) by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "going along with the current of ideas and conforming to the",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
